{#-
  privacy.html.j2: /privacy/ (Milestone 2 step 7). The text is site/content/privacy.md,
  rendered by tff_site.pages (raw HTML off). Context: every page's, plus `heading` and
  `content`. The tip section shows only once the tip link is on the site (site.tip_url, M2
  step 8), and names both of its places: the nav's Tip Jar (tip_jar, 2026-10-05) and the tip
  pitch that ends the About page's note (why_not_listed_conversation, 2026-11-21). No script:
  the page needs none. Styles: site/css/40-pages.css.
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<article class="page page-prose">
<h1>{{ heading }}</h1>
{{ content }}
{% if site.tip_url %}
<h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
<p>The Tip Jar link at the top of each page, and the tip link that ends the About page's note, go to Stripe's payment page. Nothing from Stripe loads on this site. Stripe's page, and its own privacy policy, come into play only after you click.</p>
{% endif %}
</article>
{% endblock %}
